            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, kentucky\u2019s execution protocol uses a three\u2011drug sequence: the anesthetic thiopental, the paralytic pancuronium, and the lethal potassium chloride."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether a medical doctor could participate in the execution, noting that the American Medical Association\u2019s Code of Ethics forbids such participation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 27
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Stevens, justice Stevens questioned whether the parties agree that improper administration could cause excruciating pain."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether the phlebotomist present in the execution chamber is a medical doctor."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter also asked whether the petitioners have shown a significant likelihood of excruciating pain during execution."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg questioned why the state would rely on non\u2011professional personnel to administer and monitor the drugs."
      }
    ],
