            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, petitioners argue that Kentucky\u2019s three\u2011drug lethal\u2011injection protocol (thiopental, pancuronium, potassium chloride) poses a danger of cruel and inhumane executions because inadequate anesthesia can cause conscious paralysis and excruciating pain."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, petitioners propose a single\u2011dose barbiturate protocol that would avoid the need for a medically trained professional to administer the drugs."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6e0f44b20261-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Verrilli, the dispute centers on whether the execution method violates the Eighth Amendment\u2019s prohibition on cruel and unusual punishment."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, the three\u2011drug protocol can cause a cruel and inhumane execution because inadequate anesthesia may leave the inmate conscious during paralysis and lethal injection."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 4
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, monitoring procedures to ensure the inmate is adequately anesthetized are practically nonexistent."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6e0f44b20261-0000-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 6,
                "start": 6
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Donald B. Verrilli, Jr., on behalf of the Petitioners, a single dose of barbiturate would eliminate the need for a medically trained professional to administer the drugs."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6e0f44b20261-0001-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 21,
                "start": 21
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Verrilli, the petitioners do not argue that states must choose the least painful method; they rely on three well\u2011established Eighth Amendment principles."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Verrilli",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "6e0f44b202619504b34435027801837d54f3145dcfa813c91e97e9924b862157",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-6e0f44b20261-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 57,
                "start": 57
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Verrilli, kentucky\u2019s deliberate choice of this protocol is analogous to deliberate indifference in confinement cases."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioners\u2019 Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
